    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on wolfram2002-ch01-09: not-empirically-resolvable, resolvability 0.04";
    dc:description "The assertion is a philosophical interpretation rather than a discriminating empirical claim. Data on human behavior or computational predictability cannot settle whether that behavior meaningfully constitutes free will.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    dc:type "resolution-route/none";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: No empirical decision criterion follows without first choosing a philosophical definition of meaningful free will. Behavioral unpredictability could be measured, but it would not confirm freedom rather than deterministic complexity.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Free will is not operationally defined.", "Unpredictability does not distinguish agency from deterministic irreducibility.";
